From 75f0b4747db0d9db58866389c28c2fd07b25d230 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Danielnrahimi <77234268+Danielnrahimi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 02:07:47 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix: render narration audio off the request path

The TTS endpoint called ElevenLabs while the browser waited on the socket.
A full turn takes the provider longer than the gateway allows, so the request
died at 504 and the audio element received an HTML error page as its source
(MediaError 4 / NotSupportedError) - text played, narration did not.

Audio is now rendered right after the narration commits, in the same deferred
step that already runs the LLM turn, and the endpoint either serves the cached
mp3 or answers 202 while the render finishes. The client polls for it instead
of pointing an audio element at a slow URL.
